diff --git a/tests/bc250-mesh/clip-cull-distance/README.md b/tests/bc250-mesh/clip-cull-distance/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d13cbb4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/bc250-mesh/clip-cull-distance/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,68 @@
+# clip-cull-distance: ClipDistance / CullDistance through the BC250 Mesh routes (drm-shim only)
+
+Mesh shaders that write per-vertex `gl_ClipDistance` / `gl_CullDistance` used to be refused by the split
+(`BC250 mesh split rejected: special vertex output`), so every such pipeline above the piece ceiling failed with
+`VK_ERROR_FEATURE_NOT_PRESENT` (FINAL FANTASY VII REBIRTH's 128-triangle Mesh shaders write `CullDistance[1]`).
+What the driver does now (`radv_bc250.c`, `ac_nir_lower_ngg_mesh.c`):
+
+| route | clip/cull distances |
+|---|---|
+| split (direct mesh-only split, hybrid Task replay, LDS-fit pieces) | per-vertex built-ins pass through unchanged like the position (every piece re-executes the body and writes all its vertices; only primitive arrays are sliced): ClipDistance, CullDistance and PointSize are admitted |
+| private-vertex expansion | the merged compact array (`CLIP_DIST0/1`) is copied per expanded vertex, only the elements the application writes (all of them for a dynamic index): the three copies of a triangle's corner carry the same values, so hardware clipping and culling decide as for the unexpanded shader, and the enabled distances (`PA_CL_VS_OUT_CNTL`, from the final shader's written components) are the same |
+| `RADV_BC250_MESH_DIRECT_READ` | `CLIP_DIST0/1` are direct-read locations like the position |
+| `RADV_BC250_MESH_AUTOCULL` | candidates now; survivors export their corners' distances, and a triangle with one exported clip or cull distance negative at all three corners is also culled (as VS NGG culling); the viewport index still makes a shader a non-candidate |
+| `RADV_BC250_MESH_COMPACT` (shared-vertex compaction) | every per-vertex output, the distances included, is exported from the shared vertex's source corner; with autocull the survivors are decided with the same distance test |
+| compact LDS, implicit triangles, barycentrics, raw AMD route | unchanged code paths, checked here |
+
+**Default forms since b1f639e** (the FF7 hang, `MESH_PERF/ff7hang` "Fix"): no Mesh pipeline exports a clip/cull
+distance position vector (`SPI_SHADER_POS_FORMAT` POS1/POS2, `PA_CL_VS_OUT_CNTL` CCDIST) unless
+`RADV_BC250_MESH_ALLOW_POS1=1`:
+
+| switch (default) | what |
+|---|---|
+| `RADV_BC250_MESH_CLIPCULL_CONST` (1) | constant non-negative distances (not NaN, not +Inf; `-0.0` counts as 0) are removed on the variables before every BC250 rewrite; an array left without stores is dropped with its array size. Not when the fragment shader reads the distances. |
+| `RADV_BC250_MESH_CULLDIST_CULL` (1) | remaining cull distances are culled in the shader and not exported (autocull, also without `RADV_BC250_MESH_AUTOCULL`, on every draw: no runtime skip); one-wave size rule; > 64 triangles are split for it |
+| `RADV_BC250_MESH_ALLOW_POS1` (0) | admit the clip/cull vector form (hardware gates only); otherwise a non-constant clip distance, or a cull distance autocull does not take (viewport index output, raw shapes), is refused with `BC250 Mesh pipeline refused: ...` |
+
+The GFX10 fully-culled dummy vertex exports every declared position vector. The legacy variants of the suite run with
+`RADV_BC250_MESH_ALLOW_POS1=1 RADV_BC250_MESH_CULLDIST_CULL=0` (the vector form a hardware gate would test, and the only
+one with a raw reference); the `def` / `defgame` / `defshared` / `pos` / `legconst` variants check the defaults
+(column 6 of the case table: `refuse`, `cull`, `none` with a byte-identical twin (column 7), `same`), see run.sh.
+New fixtures: `CONSTCLIP` / `CONSTCULL` with `CVAL` (constant element stores), cull-only variants of the split,
+Task, CullPrimitive, per-primitive, partial, special-value and PointSize cases, and `k80` (the culling split).
+
+Other built-ins in the split: per-primitive PrimitiveId, Layer and ViewportIndex are sliced like generic
+per-primitive attributes (the expansion already makes them flat per-vertex outputs; a fragment shader reading them
+is still refused); the primitive shading rate stays refused (GFX10.1 has no VRS; the expansion does not handle it).
+
+```sh
+ICD=<build>/src/amd/vulkan/radeon_devenv_icd.x86_64.json BUILD=<build> \
+  [OLDICD=<icd of the build before, for the identity checks>] [SEEDS=60] [KEEP=<dir>] [ONLY=<regex>] ./run.sh
+```
+
+Every Vulkan program runs inside bwrap with a fresh `/dev` (no `/dev/dri`), the noop amdgpu drm-shim and
+`AMDGPU_GPU_ID=gfx1013` (`../direct-read/pipe.c` refuses any other device). Fixtures: `cc.mesh` (`-D` options in its
+header: `NCLIP`/`NCULL` 0..8, dynamic index, sparse writes, NaN/Inf/-0.0, PointSize, per-primitive Layer /
+ViewportIndex / generic / CullPrimitive, partial counts, push constants, Task payload), `cc.frag` (optionally reads
+the clip/cull inputs and barycentrics), `cc.task`.
+
+Per case (26, plus the autocull distance-culling and shared-vertex coverage checks and three self-checks): variants off, raw (`RADV_BC250_MESH_AMD=1`, the unsplit unexpanded shader), `PERF_PIECE_PRIMS=64`,
+`DIRECT_READ=1`/`full`, `COMPACT_LDS`, `IMPLICIT_TRIS`, `RADV_BC250_MESH_COMPACT=1` alone and with autocull, autocull (with and without direct read), the game switch set
+of `run-bc250.sh` with and without autocull, and a barycentric fragment shader; each must compile and submit without
+NIR/ACO validation errors or split refusals, with the expected traces (pieces, direct read of the clip/cull slots,
+autocull applied or refused for the viewport index). The CPU oracle (`../direct-read/mesh_oracle`) then compares:
+
+- **geometry** (`--geometry --grid`): the raw shader against the split/expanded variants: the same live triangles
+  in order and, per corner, identical position, misc vector and clip/cull distance exports;
+- **pieces** (`--geometry --geometry-params`): 3 pieces against 2 pieces, parameters included;
+- **exact**: off against direct read, compact LDS and implicit triangles;
+- **autocull** (`--autocull`): the culling reference now includes the distance test; survivors must export exactly
+  their corners' distances;
+- **shared** (`--compact`, and `--compact --autocull` with autocull): the shared-vertex export's hang-safety rules on
+  adversarial index data and every corner's exports, distances included (exact where the compaction is refused, e.g.
+  CullPrimitive, per-primitive outputs, the viewport index); at least one case with distances must apply it;
+- **bary** (`--bary-ref`).
+
+Every oracle line of a case with distances must have compared clip/cull channels (`clipcull_channels`). Self-checks:
+the geometry oracle fails against a shader with one wrong distance (`SKEW`), and `--autocull --mutate 6` (no distance
+test) fails, alone and with `--compact`. With `OLDICD`, the cases without distances are byte-identical to that build in every variant.
diff --git a/tests/bc250-mesh/clip-cull-distance/cc.frag b/tests/bc250-mesh/clip-cull-distance/cc.frag
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..239dbef
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/bc250-mesh/clip-cull-distance/cc.frag
@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+#version 460
+/* Reads every generic output of cc.mesh for the same -D options; FSCLIP also reads the interpolated
+ * gl_ClipDistance / gl_CullDistance inputs, BARY the barycentric coordinates. */
+#if BARY
+#extension GL_EXT_fragment_shader_barycentric : require
+#endif
+#if PERPRIM
+#extension GL_EXT_mesh_shader : require
+#endif
+#ifndef NCLIP
+#define NCLIP 0
+#endif
+#ifndef NCULL
+#define NCULL 0
+#endif
+#if FSCLIP && NCLIP
+in float gl_ClipDistance[NCLIP];
+#endif
+#if FSCLIP && NCULL
+in float gl_CullDistance[NCULL];
+#endif
+layout(location = 0) in vec4 v0;
+layout(location = 1) flat in uint v1;
+#if PERPRIM
+layout(location = 2) perprimitiveEXT flat in vec4 pp0;
+#endif
+layout(location = 0) out vec4 o0;
+void main()
+{
+   vec4 r = v0 + vec4(float(v1));
+#if PERPRIM
+   r += pp0;
+#endif
+#if FSCLIP && NCLIP
+   r.x += gl_ClipDistance[0];
+#endif
+#if FSCLIP && NCULL
+   r.y += gl_CullDistance[NCULL - 1];
+#endif
+#if BARY
+   r.xyz += gl_BaryCoordEXT;
+#endif
+   o0 = r;
+}
diff --git a/tests/bc250-mesh/clip-cull-distance/cc.mesh b/tests/bc250-mesh/clip-cull-distance/cc.mesh
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..2208b82
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/bc250-mesh/clip-cull-distance/cc.mesh
@@ -0,0 +1,241 @@
+#version 460
+#extension GL_EXT_mesh_shader : require
+/* Clip/cull distance fixtures (run.sh), one per set of -D options:
+ *   LANES/VERTS/PRIMS : workgroup size, max vertices, max primitives (defaults 64/64/64); with VERTS or
+ *                       PRIMS > LANES every lane writes its vertices / primitives in a loop.
+ *   NCLIP / NCULL     : gl_ClipDistance[NCLIP] / gl_CullDistance[NCULL] (NCLIP + NCULL <= 8), every element
+ *                       written for every vertex. Values: small signed steps (some triangles have one
+ *                       distance negative at all three corners), -0.0, and with SPECIAL a NaN and +-Inf.
+ *   DYN               : the distances are written in a loop with a dynamic element index.
+ *   SPARSE            : only the even elements are written (the odd ones stay undefined).
+ *   PSIZ              : also writes gl_PointSize (a triangle mesh: exported, ignored by the rasterizer).
+ *   LAYER / VIEWPORT  : per-primitive gl_Layer / gl_ViewportIndex (split: sliced like generic attributes).
+ *   PERPRIM           : a per-primitive flat vec4 (the expansion's flat attribute path).
+ *   CULLPRIM          : gl_CullPrimitiveEXT on every 5th primitive (the split's cull compaction).
+ *   PARTIAL           : fewer vertices/primitives than declared, from the workgroup id.
+ *   PC                : the workgroup base comes from a push constant.
+ *   TASK              : launched by cc.task (hybrid Task replay); reads the payload.
+ *   SKEW              : oracle self-check only: the last distance of vertex 5 is off by one.
+ *   CONSTCLIP / CONSTCULL : every ClipDistance / CullDistance element written is the constant CVAL
+ *                       (default 0.0, FINAL FANTASY VII REBIRTH's CullDistance) instead of dist():
+ *                       RADV_BC250_MESH_CLIPCULL_CONST removes it when CVAL >= 0 (not NaN, not +Inf).
+ * Primitive indices are always below the vertex count (the oracle's geometry mode compares the raw,
+ * unsplit shader with the split and expanded ones: both must see valid geometry). */
+#ifndef LANES
+#define LANES 64
+#endif
+#ifndef VERTS
+#define VERTS 64
+#endif
+#ifndef PRIMS
+#define PRIMS 64
+#endif
+#ifndef NCLIP
+#define NCLIP 0
+#endif
+#ifndef NCULL
+#define NCULL 0
+#endif
+#ifndef CVAL
+#define CVAL 0.0
+#endif
+layout(local_size_x = LANES) in;
+layout(max_vertices = VERTS, max_primitives = PRIMS, triangles) out;
+layout(push_constant) uniform PCB { uint base; uint n; uint m; uint k; } pc;
+
+out gl_MeshPerVertexEXT {
+   vec4 gl_Position;
+#if PSIZ
+   float gl_PointSize;
+#endif
+#if NCLIP
+   float gl_ClipDistance[NCLIP];
+#endif
+#if NCULL
+   float gl_CullDistance[NCULL];
+#endif
+} gl_MeshVerticesEXT[];
+
+#if LAYER || VIEWPORT || CULLPRIM
+perprimitiveEXT out gl_MeshPerPrimitiveEXT {
+#if LAYER
+   int gl_Layer;
+#endif
+#if VIEWPORT
+   int gl_ViewportIndex;
+#endif
+#if CULLPRIM
+   bool gl_CullPrimitiveEXT;
+#endif
+} gl_MeshPrimitivesEXT[];
+#endif
+
+#if TASK
+struct P { uint base; };
+taskPayloadSharedEXT P payload;
+#endif
+
+layout(location = 0) out vec4 v0[];
+layout(location = 1) flat out uint v1[];
+#if PERPRIM
+layout(location = 2) perprimitiveEXT flat out vec4 pp0[];
+#endif
+
+float dist(uint v, uint i, uint g)
+{
+   uint h = v * 5u + i * 3u + g;
+#if SPECIAL
+   if (h % 17u == 4u)
+      return uintBitsToFloat(0x7fc00000u);
+   if (h % 19u == 6u)
+      return uintBitsToFloat(i % 2u == 0u ? 0xff800000u : 0x7f800000u);
+#endif
+   if (h % 11u == 0u)
+      return -0.0;
+#if SKEW
+   if (v == 5u && i == uint(NCLIP + NCULL - 1))
+      return (float(h % 7u) - 3.0) * 0.5 + float(i) * 0.125;
+#endif
+   return (float(h % 7u) - 4.0) * 0.5 + float(i) * 0.125;
+}
+
+void main()
+{
+   uint i = gl_LocalInvocationIndex;
+   uint g = gl_WorkGroupID.x;
+#if PC
+   g += pc.base;
+#endif
+#if TASK
+   g += payload.base;
+#endif
+   uint nv = VERTS, np = PRIMS;
+#if PARTIAL
+   nv = VERTS - (g % 3u);
+   np = PRIMS - (g % 5u);
+#endif
+   SetMeshOutputsEXT(nv, np);
+
+#if VERTS > LANES
+   for (uint v = i; v < VERTS; v += LANES)
+#else
+   uint v = i;
+   if (v < VERTS)
+#endif
+   {
+      float f = float(v);
+      float x = fract(sin(f * 12.9898 + float(g) * 78.233) * 43758.5453) * 2.4 - 1.2;
+      float y = fract(sin(f * 39.3468 + float(g) * 11.135) * 24634.6345) * 2.4 - 1.2;
+      float w = (v % 23u == 7u) ? -0.5 : 1.0 + f / float(VERTS);
+      gl_MeshVerticesEXT[v].gl_Position = vec4(x * w, y * w, 0.5, w);
+#if PSIZ
+      gl_MeshVerticesEXT[v].gl_PointSize = 1.0 + f;
+#endif
+#if DYN
+      for (uint e = 0u; e < uint(NCLIP + NCULL); e++) {
+#if NCLIP
+         if (e < uint(NCLIP))
+            gl_MeshVerticesEXT[v].gl_ClipDistance[e] = dist(v, e, g);
+#endif
+#if NCULL
+         if (e >= uint(NCLIP))
+            gl_MeshVerticesEXT[v].gl_CullDistance[e - uint(NCLIP)] = dist(v, e, g);
+#endif
+      }
+#else
+#if NCLIP && CONSTCLIP
+      /* Constant element indices (no loop), as a compiler emits them for a fixed-size array. */
+#if NCLIP > 0
+      gl_MeshVerticesEXT[v].gl_ClipDistance[0] = CVAL;
+#endif
+#if NCLIP > 1 && !SPARSE
+      gl_MeshVerticesEXT[v].gl_ClipDistance[1] = CVAL;
+#endif
+#if NCLIP > 2
+      gl_MeshVerticesEXT[v].gl_ClipDistance[2] = CVAL;
+#endif
+#if NCLIP > 3 && !SPARSE
+      gl_MeshVerticesEXT[v].gl_ClipDistance[3] = CVAL;
+#endif
+#if NCLIP > 4
+      gl_MeshVerticesEXT[v].gl_ClipDistance[4] = CVAL;
+#endif
+#if NCLIP > 5 && !SPARSE
+      gl_MeshVerticesEXT[v].gl_ClipDistance[5] = CVAL;
+#endif
+#if NCLIP > 6
+      gl_MeshVerticesEXT[v].gl_ClipDistance[6] = CVAL;
+#endif
+#if NCLIP > 7 && !SPARSE
+      gl_MeshVerticesEXT[v].gl_ClipDistance[7] = CVAL;
+#endif
+#elif NCLIP
+      for (int e = 0; e < NCLIP; e++)
+#if SPARSE
+         if (e % 2 == 0)
+#endif
+         gl_MeshVerticesEXT[v].gl_ClipDistance[e] = dist(v, uint(e), g);
+#endif
+#if NCULL && CONSTCULL
+#if NCULL > 0
+      gl_MeshVerticesEXT[v].gl_CullDistance[0] = CVAL;
+#endif
+#if NCULL > 1 && !SPARSE
+      gl_MeshVerticesEXT[v].gl_CullDistance[1] = CVAL;
+#endif
+#if NCULL > 2
+      gl_MeshVerticesEXT[v].gl_CullDistance[2] = CVAL;
+#endif
+#if NCULL > 3 && !SPARSE
+      gl_MeshVerticesEXT[v].gl_CullDistance[3] = CVAL;
+#endif
+#if NCULL > 4
+      gl_MeshVerticesEXT[v].gl_CullDistance[4] = CVAL;
+#endif
+#if NCULL > 5 && !SPARSE
+      gl_MeshVerticesEXT[v].gl_CullDistance[5] = CVAL;
+#endif
+#if NCULL > 6
+      gl_MeshVerticesEXT[v].gl_CullDistance[6] = CVAL;
+#endif
+#if NCULL > 7 && !SPARSE
+      gl_MeshVerticesEXT[v].gl_CullDistance[7] = CVAL;
+#endif
+#elif NCULL
+      for (int e = 0; e < NCULL; e++)
+#if SPARSE
+         if (e % 2 == 0)
+#endif
+         gl_MeshVerticesEXT[v].gl_CullDistance[e] = dist(v, uint(e + NCLIP), g);
+#endif
+#endif
+      v0[v] = vec4(f, x, float(g), 1.0 + f);
+      v1[v] = v ^ g;
+   }
+
+#if PRIMS > LANES
+   for (uint p = i; p < PRIMS; p += LANES)
+#else
+   uint p = i;
+   if (p < PRIMS)
+#endif
+   {
+      uint lim = max(nv, 1u);
+      uint a = p % lim;
+      uint b = (p * 7u + g + 1u) % lim;
+      uint c = (lim - 1u) - ((p * 3u + g) % lim);
+      gl_PrimitiveTriangleIndicesEXT[p] = uvec3(a, b, c);
+#if LAYER
+      gl_MeshPrimitivesEXT[p].gl_Layer = int((p + g) % 4u);
+#endif
+#if VIEWPORT
+      gl_MeshPrimitivesEXT[p].gl_ViewportIndex = int((p * 3u + g) % 2u);
+#endif
+#if CULLPRIM
+      gl_MeshPrimitivesEXT[p].gl_CullPrimitiveEXT = (p % 5u) == 3u;
+#endif
+#if PERPRIM
+      pp0[p] = vec4(float(p), float(g), float(a), float(c));
+#endif
+   }
+}
